-- title:
--   Étale part of the pinned Tate point descends under qmapstoq^q
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, $A$ a valuation subring of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, and $A_0 :=$ `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` the valuation subring of the intermediate field $k_0 \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$ obtained by pulling $A$ back.
--
--   *Arithmetic data and local hypotheses.* A prime $q$ with $5 \le q$; a natural number $M' \ne 0$ with $q \nmid M'$; a valuation subring $A \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$. The local hypotheses on $A_0$ are: `hdvr`, that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; `hunif`, that the maximal ideal of $A_0$ is generated by $\pi_0$; `hhens`, that $A_0$ is a Henselian local ring; `hres`, that the residue field of $A_0$ is algebraically closed; and `hκ`, that every $a \in A$ admits $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ and $a - c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ (so $k_0 \cap A$ already exhausts the residue field of $A$).
--
--   *The auxiliary prime and the root of unity.* A prime $\ell'$ with $\ell' \ne q$, $3 \le \ell'$ and $\ell' \nmid M'$; an element $\xi \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell'$-th root of unity; and `hιξ`, the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$.
--
--   *The two function fields.* $K$ is an intermediate field of $k_0((\mathfrak q))/k_0$ (Laurent series over $k_0$) required by `hK` to be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ')^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ') M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), that is, the subfield of $k_0((\mathfrak q))$ generated over $k_0$ by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell')^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q\ell')^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell'$. Likewise $K''$ is required by `hK''` to be the corresponding field at level $\ell'^2M'$ with $H$ the units of $\mathbb Z/\ell'^2M'$ congruent to $1$ modulo $\ell'$. Both $K$ and $K''$ carry $A_0$-algebra structures compatible with $k_0$. Finally, `hj` provides an element $j \in K$ whose image in $k_0((\mathfrak q))$ is the coefficient embedding of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant, together with $j \ne 0$.
--
--   *Functoriality hypotheses.* `hℓ` asserts that over every $A_0$-algebra $T$, a Katz level-$\ell'$ structure ([`ModularCurve.IsLevelPStructure`](def/ModularCurve_KatzLevelP.html#L104): both marked points satisfy the affine equation, both $x$-coordinates are roots of `preΨ ℓ'`, and the two independence elements are units) is preserved by Weierstrass variable changes, in the sense that $C \bullet W$ carries `D.variableChange C`. `hM` asserts the analogous statement for [`ModularCurve.IsGamma0PowAt W p k h`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassGamma0Pow.html#L55) and the transformed polynomial `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h`. `hVC` and `hCO` assert that, over every $A_0$-algebra (resp. every $A_0$-algebra map $f$), the projective model of a Weierstrass curve admits a graded ring homomorphism $\varphi$ realising the variable change $C$ (resp. the coefficient change $f$) in the sense of `IsVariableChangeHom` (resp. `IsCoefficientHom`), subject to the containment of the irrelevant ideal of the target in the image under $\varphi$ of the irrelevant ideal of the source.
--
--   *Group laws and level transport.* A family of relative group laws $\mathcal G$ on projective Weierstrass models over $A_0$-algebras, with `h𝒢` that it is chord–tangent (a points evaluation exists in each case) and `h𝒢O` that its identity section is the origin (a chart homomorphism killing $x/y$ and $z/y$); a level transport $\mathcal T$ for $\mathcal G$ at $q$, with `h𝒯` asserting `IsSectionTransport`, i.e. compatibility of the transported Drinfeld sections $P, Q$ with variable changes and with coefficient changes through the corresponding graded homomorphisms.
--
--   Let $\mathcal R :=$ [`WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.rigidDataPow A₀ ℓ' M' q hℓ hM 𝒢 𝒯`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassGamma0Pow.html#L93), the rigid Weierstrass datum attached to the product level component $\Gamma_0(M')$-polynomials $\times$ (Katz level-$\ell'$ data $\times$ Drinfeld level-$q$ pair); a raw object of $\mathcal R$ over a ring $T$ consists of a Weierstrass curve with unit discriminant together with a level object of that product satisfying the corresponding level predicates.
--
--   *The pinned Tate point.* $x_0$ is a point of $\mathcal R$ over $K$, subject to `hx₀`: its $j$-invariant, viewed in $k_0((\mathfrak q))$, equals [`ModularCurve.jqNModC k₀ (q*ℓ')`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), the image of the $j$-expansion under $\mathfrak q \mapsto \mathfrak q^{q\ell'}$. The pinning hypothesis `hμ` asserts the existence of a variable change $C$ over $k_0((\mathfrak q))$ and of a raw $\mathcal R$-object $r$ over $K$ with class $x_0$, such that: the unit $C.u$ satisfies $C.u\,(2x_\xi + \tfrac16) = 2y_\xi + x_\xi$, where $(x_\xi, y_\xi) =$ [`ModularCurve.cuspPoint k₀ (q*ℓ')`](def/ModularCurve_KatzLevelPCusps.html#L59) at $\xi$ and the vector $(1,0)$ (hence the toric point at $\xi$), while $C.r = -\tfrac1{12}$, $C.s = -\tfrac12$, $C.t = \tfrac1{24}$ as constant Hahn series; the curve of $r$, base-changed to $k_0((\mathfrak q))$, equals $C \bullet$ [`ModularCurve.tateBase k₀ (q*ℓ')`](def/ModularCurve_TateSlots.html#L46); for every prime $p \mid M'$, every field $F'$ with a ring homomorphism $f : k_0 \to F'$ and every primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta \in F'$, the $p$-th $\Gamma_0$-polynomial of $r$, pushed to $F'((\mathfrak q))$, equals the `kernelVariableChangeDeg` twist by $C$ (in degree `gamma0PowDeg p (v_p(M'))`) of $\prod_a (X - x(\zeta^a))$, the product over $1 \le a \le p^{v_p(M')}/2$ with $p \nmid a$ of the $x$-coordinates of the toric points [`ModularCurve.toricPoint F' (q*ℓ') (ζ^a)`](def/ModularCurve_TateSlots.html#L125); the Katz level-$\ell'$ slot of $r$, pushed to $k_0((\mathfrak q))$, equals the $C$-twist of [`ModularCurve.cuspData k₀ (q*ℓ')`](def/ModularCurve_KatzLevelPCusps.html#L71) at the vectors $(q,0)$ and $(0,-q)$ in $\mathbb Z/q\ell'$; and there are $P_x, P_y, Q_x, Q_y \in K$ whose images in $k_0((\mathfrak q))$ are the four coordinates $x_P, y_P, x_Q, y_Q$ of the $C$-twist of [`ModularCurve.cuspData k₀ (q*ℓ')`](def/ModularCurve_KatzLevelPCusps.html#L71) at the vectors $(\ell',0)$ and $(0,-\ell')$, and such that the Drinfeld sections $P$ and $Q$ of $r$ pass through $(P_x,P_y)$ and $(Q_x,Q_y)$ in the sense of `IsSectionThrough` (a $Z$-chart section homomorphism with these affine coordinates).
--
--   *Conclusion.* There exist a raw $\mathcal R$-object $r$ over $K$ and a raw object $r''$ over $K''$ for the étale datum
--   $$\big((\text{gamma0PowComponent } A_0\, M') \times ((\text{levelPComponent } A_0\, \ell') \times \text{trivial})\big)^{\mathrm{rigid}},$$
--   whose third slot is the one-point type, such that, writing $E$ for the composite of the inclusion $K'' \hookrightarrow k_0((\mathfrak q))$ with [`ModularCurve.qExpand k₀ q`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25) (the substitution $\mathfrak q \mapsto \mathfrak q^{q}$):
--
--   1. the class of $r$ in the point set of $\mathcal R$ over $K$ is $x_0$;
--
--   2. the curve of $r$, base-changed along $K \hookrightarrow k_0((\mathfrak q))$, equals the curve of $r''$ pushed forward along $E$;
--
--   3. for every prime factor $p$ of $M'$, the $p$-th $\Gamma_0$-polynomial of $r$, mapped along $K \hookrightarrow k_0((\mathfrak q))$, equals the $p$-th $\Gamma_0$-polynomial of $r''$ mapped along $E$;
--
--   4. the Katz level-$\ell'$ data of $r$, mapped along $K \hookrightarrow k_0((\mathfrak q))$, equals the Katz level-$\ell'$ data of $r''$ mapped along $E$.
--
--   No assertion is made about the Drinfeld level-$q$ slot of $r$, and the representative $r$ produced here need not be the one furnished by `hμ`.
--
--   This is the descent step showing that the étale part — curve, $\Gamma_0(M')$-kernel polynomials and Katz $\Gamma(\ell')$-coordinates — of the pinned Tate point at full level $(q\ell')^2M'$ is the substitution $\mathfrak q \mapsto \mathfrak q^{q}$ of a genuine level-$\ell'^2M'$ structure over the smaller Laurent field $K''$, the level-$q$ Drinfeld data being deliberately left out of the comparison. It is used in the identification of the $q$-expansion charts at the Mazur cusp in the full-level specialisation argument, via [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.eq_of_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_of_forall_coe_eq_qExpand_iff_chartAlgFin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.eq_of_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_of_forall_coe_eq_qExpand_iff_chartAlgFin), and rests on the Tate-curve substitution identities [`ModularCurve.tateBase_mul_eq_map_qExpand_and_tateToricPoint_eq_and_nonToricPoint_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.tateBase_mul_eq_map_qExpand_and_tateToricPoint_eq_and_nonToricPoint_eq) together with the normalised full-level Tate representative supplied by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_variableChange_raw_etale_tate_weightOne_level_fst_gamma0Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_variableChange_raw_etale_tate_weightOne_level_fst_gamma0Pow).
